Right.  The stairs trick is only part of a working strategy to kill
Yeenoghu.  For *every* monster there's a strategy that can be
figured out to kill him using a weaker player.
















& Yeenoghu 56 18 -5 80 fp W3d6 W2d8c W1d6. M2d6M 

W3d6 means 3 6-sided dice of regular physical damage.
W2d8c means 2 8-sided dice of confusion.
W1d6. means 1 6-sided die of paralysis.
M2d6M means 2 6-sided dice of magic missle spell.

With an AC of -5 Yeenoghu isn't all that hard to take out
once you have a powerfull weapon.  To best fight him
takes an AC under -5 to better his, a unihorn to counter
the confusion, a ring of free action to counter the
paralysis, and any source of MR to counter the magic
missiles.

Basically once you have MR, good armor, a unihorn and a
good weapon it can be time to take him out.  One good
way is to use a scroll of earth to build a fort and to
fight from within it with daggers and wands.  Build the
fort on the upstairs so he can't retreat.  Bounce up
and down healing.  When you run out of ammunition wade
in and finish him off.

As long as you're on the upstairs, either being able to
make a fort of having free action is enough once you
have a unihorn and MR.

